{
        ERR_clear_error();
        UNUSED_ARG(shatype);

        if(shatype == SHATYPE_SHA256) {
...
```

The `UNUSED_ARG(shatype)` is called, but then `shatype` is used. This is fine.

But here's the thing - what if `shatype` is `SHATYPE_SHA1`? Then it falls through to the `else` branch:
```c
        } else
          if (!HMAC(EVP_sha1(), key, (int)keylen, buf, len, hmac, hmac_len)) {
            return -1;
          }
```

This calls `HMAC(EVP_sha1(), ...)` which writes 20 bytes. So `new_hmac[0..19]` is initialized.

